 "definitions": {
  "shock": "An S&P 500 member's own part of a session -- its return less what its market (SPY) and sector-fund betas explain -- at least 2 of its own volatilities, down or up. Volatility from the 60 sessions before, betas from the 252 before; nothing is estimated with the day itself or later.",
  "outcome": "The own part from the next session's open to the close 1, 5 or 20 sessions after the shock, so a reader could have acted on it. Mean and median across the group's shocks; positive share is the share of shocks that ended above zero; the interval is a 95% bootstrap resampling whole months.",
  "reported": "The company's earnings report fell in that session's reaction (before the open, or after the previous close).",
  "gap_led": "The gap from the previous close to the open was at least as large as the move from the open to the close.",
  "repeat": "Another shock of the same sign in the 10 sessions before.",
  "vix_high": "VIX closed above its median of the 252 sessions before.",
  "stock_above_200d": "The stock closed above its 200-session average.",
  "market_above_200d": "SPY closed above its 200-session average."
 },
